The function open:creib.forge.conformance.records.recover_json_object, under its documented rule 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text', should return {"a": 1} for the first reply (a javascript-fenced object followed by a bare object) and {"b": 2} for the second reply (just the bare object); the check that gives {"b": 2} for both is incorrect because it fails to recognize the javascript fence as holding an object.